# What is said at the things they do together: dice, the flask, a story, the
# watch changing, the captain's round, waking the sleeper, feeding the fire.

== round_tam
place: round
cast: A = captain; B = name(Tam)
cooldown: once
A [kicks]: On your feet. The Moon-Glass doesn't guard itself.
B: I was listening, Captain. With my eyes shut.

# Asking the others first (played by the gathering itself, never chosen).

== invite_dice
place: invite
cast: A = any; B = any
cooldown: 0s
again: yes
A: Dice?
B: Go on, then.

== invite_flask
place: invite
cast: A = any; B = any
cooldown: 0s
again: yes
A [nods]: Something to keep the cold out?
B: I thought you'd never ask.

== invite_story
place: invite
cast: A = any; B = any
cooldown: 0s
again: yes
A: Sit down, you lot. I'll tell you one.
B: Not the one about the eel-wife.

# Dice at the crate by the bench.

== dice_cold_hands
place: dice
group: dice
cast: A = any; B = any; C? = any
cooldown: 10m
A [throws]: Come on, come on...
B [laughs]: Two ones. The dog's eyes.
A: My hands are too cold to throw.
C: They were warm enough for the pie.
B: Throw again, then. I'll wait.

== dice_col_wins
place: dice
group: dice
cast: A = lucky; B = any; C? = any
cooldown: 10m
A [throws]: Sixes. Both of them.
B: Again? Let me see those bones.
A [shrugs]: Same bones as yours.
C [laughs]: Nobody's luck lasts like {A}'s.
B {if craven}: I'm not betting the rest. Not against him.
B: One more. Double or nothing.

== dice_debt
place: dice
group: dice
cast: A = any; B = owes(A); C? = any
cooldown: 10m
A: You still owe me four pennies for the dice.
B: Three. I won the last throw.
A: You knocked the cup over. That's not winning, that's clumsy.
B [shrugs]: It's a kind of winning.
C [laughs]: Pay the man, {B}.

# The flask, passed between two.

== flask_brother
place: flask
cast: A = any; B = any
cooldown: 5m
A: Here. Against the cold.
B [drinks]: Gods, what is that?
A: My brother-in-law makes it.
B: Tell him to stop.
A [laughs]: Give it back, then.

== flask_just_one
place: flask
cast: A = any; B = any
cooldown: 5m
A [drinks]: Want some?
B: If the captain smells it on me...
A: She'll smell the cold on you first.
B [drinks]: Just the one.
A: That's what you said last night.

# A story round the fire.

== story_sewer_thing
place: story
cast: A = storyteller|rank>=2; B = any; C? = any; D? = any
cooldown: once
A: When I caught rats in the Undertown, we had a saying.
B: Don't fall in?
A: Don't count the eyes.
C: What eyes?
A [points:the well]: Down there, a lantern shows you eyes. Rats. Hundreds.
A: One night I counted. And one pair didn't blink.
D {if craven}: {A}, stop it.
B: What was it?
A [shrugs]: Never found out. I stopped counting.
C [laughs]: He stopped catching rats, too.
A [laughs]: That I did.

== story_captain_hask
place: story
cast: A = storyteller|rank>=2; B = any; C? = any; D? = any
cooldown: once
A: Before this captain we had old Hask. You remember Hask?
B: Only the stories.
A: He slept in his armour. Said a man should be ready.
C: Was he?
A: The night the Low Bridge burned, he stood up so fast he fell down the stairs.
B [laughs]: In his armour?
A: Rolled all the way to the gate. Loudest thing that night.
D: What happened to him?
A [shrugs]: A farm, out past the walls. Wears the armour to the privy, I hear.
C [laughs]: Ready for anything.

== story_drowned_lantern
place: story
cast: A = storyteller|rank>=2; B = any; C? = any; D? = any
cooldown: once
A: You know why they call it the Drowned Lantern?
B: Because the beer's water?
A [laughs]: Besides that. Forty years back, the canal rose in one night.
A: The keeper stayed at his post with the lantern, for the boats.
C: And drowned?
A: They found the lantern still burning on the roof. Never found him.
B [whispers]: They say it's still lit, some nights.
A: They say you owe me a drink for the story, too.
D [laughs]: Now that's a ghost story.
